"map\nTHE MEMORY MAP, AS THIS IMAGE MEASURES IT\n  this image      00200000 to 0081AB73   6400884 bytes, measured from the image itself\n  reserved        00200000 to 008FFFFF   this monitor's code, measured from the image\n  reserved        0D000000 to 0F6FFFFF   its variables, placed by --bss-addr\n  reserved        001FF000 to 001FFFFF   the autoboot record\n  reserved        08A00000 to 091FFFFF   the DSI framebuffer\n  reserved        001FC000 to 001FEFFF   the reserved raw-secondary stacks\n  reserved        09200000 to 099FFFFF   the driver-module arena and its staging window\n  reserved        001FB000 to 001FBFFF   the boot phase record\n  reserved        0B000000 to 0BBFFFFF   the screenshot capture area\n  reserved        10000000 to 13FFFFFF   the reserved Vulkan device-memory heap\n  its stack top   00100000               and it grows downwards from there\n  stage a file at 00900000               which is what the upload tools ask for\n\nWhere a payload may go:\n  the low window   00900000 to 07EFFFFF   (about 118 MB)\n  the high window  40000000 to FBFFFFFF   (about 3 GB)\n  Nothing in this map is a constant this program was told. The\n  monitor's extent is the size of the image the firmware loaded, and\n  the low window begins above it, so both move when this program\n  does. There is no maximum size.\nok\npmf> "